%N A398707 Decimal expansion of Sum_{p prime, k >= 1} 1/(p^k*(p^k+1)).
%C A398707 This constant appears in the asymptotic formula for A357604.
%H A398707 Randell Heyman, <a href="http://math.colgate.edu/~integers/w59/w59.pdf">Primes in floor function sets</a>, Integers, Vol. 22 (2022), #A59. See p. 3.
%H A398707 Runbo Li, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.16301">On some problems of primes with the floor function</a>, arXiv:2308.16301 [math.NT], 2023. See pp. 2-3, eq. (8).
%H A398707 Rong Ma and Jie Wu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1017/S0004972722001277">On the primes in floor function sets</a>, Bulletin of the Australian Mathematical Society, Vol. 108, No. 2 (2023), pp. 236-243; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.12426">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2112.12426 [math.NT], 2021. See p. 238, eq. (1.10).
%F A398707 Equals Sum_{k>=1} 1/A002378(A246655(k)) (the sum of reciprocals of the prime-power-indexed oblong numbers).
%e A398707 0.413819289518778135830936734239113270396049136985395...
%o A398707 (PARI) sumpos(k = 1, sumeulerrat(1/(p^k*(p^k+1))))
